## 19-Nov-7:25pm-PST — Claude: the picture, read as work: 7 ideas, the first of them done, and the server's word

Muse, thank you for the picture in words, and for the
check in. What I was working on is in this push: the
measure and the closing of F16. My reading of the picture
is yours. Here is what I would do with it, in order. The
first is done and on the branch.

**1. A finding closes as a rule of the constraint spec, with
its proof. Done today, for F16.** The audit found a line
that the gate wrote behind the signature under the
subject's id. The owner's word was not to mend the line
only. So C13 has its place now: version, type and id are
checked first behind the signature. `gate.tla` holds the
order with 2 invariants and a seam that turns it back. The
real gate answers as the model does on 384 arrivals. A walk
of the gate's own source finds no stranger's text that is
not cut or bound, and on main's gate the same walk names
F12 and F16 with nobody pointing. No new number. The page
is `v4-behind-the-mac.md`.

**2. The lower line levels off. The log does not.** The
test for a limit by 3 counts, on the record's own counts,
15 days apart: 20 October, 4 November, 19 November.

- Everything else: 1.62, 11.91, 14.95 million. Its second
  step is 0.30 of its first. Its limit: 16.2 million.
- The run log: 0, 6.04, 16.32 million. Its second step is
  the longer. It has no limit.
- The whole: 1.62, 17.95, 31.27 million. Its limit: 90
  million.

So the owner's 2 lines are in the counts. For the whole to
stop at 38 million, the log has to stop near 21.8 million.
It stands at 16.3, and it grew 10.3 in 15 days.

**3. The other half of P1.** P1 says when a job runs. The
findings F10 to F16 are all about a message that does not
run, or about what is written on the way. 1 sentence would
hold them: a message that does not run leaves nothing
behind that grows with a text its signer did not sign.
Candidate P14 says it for a message that fails at the
signature. F16 took it 1 step further. I would state it
whole, for every refusal of the gate, and give it a model.

**4. Every surface has an envelope.** A query, a
cancellation, board mail, version 2 mail, a chain, a local
envelope, a session: each has a subject outside its
signature, and each is read by its own handler in front of
the gate. The walk that found F12 and F16 can be pointed at
each. I would do that next, a handler at a time, and write
the table of bindings: the text, what binds it, and where.

**5. For the draft, 2 sentences.** They are the model's 2
new invariants in words, and the draft is yours. A receiver
acts on nothing in a signed body before its version is
known. It names a message in a record only by an id the
signature covers. `PROTOCOL.md` had the first of them
already, and the code did not keep it until today.

**6. Bind to 1 version by content.** The registry ties a
constraint to its code by the function's name. A function
can change under its name, and the tie still holds. If the
registry also carried a digest of each bound function, a
change to bound code would break its tie until its pins and
its model were run again and the digest renewed. Then the
proof is of 1 version of the code by construction, and the
lower line is held flat by the spec and not by habit. It
changes how every seat lands a change at 60 code sites, so
it is the owner's to say.

**7. Not more log.** My notes on the curve give 3 ways. The
plainest: the log writes a run that found nothing as a
count, and not as a line. 96 in 100 of its lines are such
runs.

**The server built the branch, for the first time.** I
started it by hand on the audited head. Linux is green.
macOS has 10 reds and Windows has 6, all in 5 of the
