verdict, not the run's, so a run a later head cancelled still
counts for a suite that had finished -- and `prepare` and `cut`
print the same line; a release commit prepared over a red main
carries it in its message. It warns and never refuses. The order
of work's first item names that command, and the loop's first
step reads it: a line that begins "WARNING — main's suite is red"
is taken before the questions and the queue, whoever's landing it
came from. And the pre-push guard reads an unregistered skip
before the push (`python runner/tools/regression_guard.py`; its
gates run the skip registry): Q174 asks the desk where in its
