Recorded, not acted on: the engine enforces single-use
tickets on both bindings while version 1's text says SHOULD
for the datagram binding. Either version 1's next revision
follows the code or the code grows a per-binding switch;
that is a version 1 question, out of this pass.

### Render, idnits, counts

The draft was re-rendered with its header pipeline: .xml,
.txt, .html, 0 warnings, and every edit verified in the
rendered text. idnits 3.3.0 ran in normal mode, offline,
against the .txt and the .xml; the report stands beside the
source. It reports 3 errors — the abstract's references to
sections and to version 1, and RFC 8446 listed as obsolete
(succeeded by RFC 9846) — all submission-time edits; its
`[HOMING-PIGEON]` warning is the tool reading the subject
marker as a citation, the same reading the version 1 reports
carry. The TLS citation is a family-wide question for the
next revision of each draft and is not changed here. Tests,
full unfiltered runs on this tree: the version 3 module 82,
OK, 0 skips; the touched batch (DTLS engine, fuzz, IPv6,
